 "notes": [
  "Engineering Solutions sold May 2, 2023; ES segment printed with zero for the quarter.",
  "IS \"Other expense (income), net\" printed 19 (expense) -> oth_inc -19. \"Loss (gain) on dispositions\" printed 1 -> gain_disp -1. Segment-table total expenses 2,262 = IS expenses 2,264 + loss on dispositions 1 - equity income 3.",
  "Exhibit 5 \"Adjusted Other (Income) Expense\" shows a non-GAAP adjustment of (23) (other expense 19 -> adjusted other income (4)) with no footnote describing it and no after-tax amount. The FY2024 10-K (Note: retirement plans) identifies a $23M pre-tax non-cash U.S. retirement plan pension settlement charge in 2023. Item recorded with pre 23 and net omitted (not printed); hence start_ni + items_net + amort check does not tie (missing after-tax pension amount); the printed aggregate after-tax line (items_total_net) does tie.",
  "MI acquisition-related costs $69M ($69M after-tax) in Q4-23. Items with after-tax \"less than $1 million\" (Indices IHS Markit merger costs $1M) recorded with net 0.",
  "Equity in income non-GAAP adjustment: asset impairment $2M ($2M after-tax), seg EQ.",
  "ngaap.items_total_pre = operating-level \"Non-GAAP adjustments\" (Exhibit 5 Total SPGI OP, 226); other (income) expense adjustment 23 and interest adjustment 7 (premium amortization benefit) printed separately. items_total_net/ps from NI/EPS reconciliation (202 / 0.64): 579 + 202 + 208 = 989 vs printed 988 (rounding).",
  "Segment rounding: MI 115+130+140=385 vs adj 386; Ratings 442+4+2=448 vs adj 447.",
  "Non-GAAP adjusted tax line: non-GAAP adjustments 41, deal-related amortization 66. adj_oth_inc = adjusted other (income) expense, net printed (4) -> +4 income.",
  "cfpub: twelve-month (ytd 12); capex and nci_dist positive outflows; three-month FCF in fcf_pub_q / adj_fcf_pub_q.",
  "Guidance (FY2024): outlook table and Exhibit 9 give GAAP diluted EPS $10.70-$10.95; the headline bullet and text say $10.65-$10.90 (inconsistency in release; table value recorded). Exhibit 9 bridge: deal amortization 2.77, IHS Markit merger costs 0.28, premium amortization benefit (0.07), restructuring 0.09, tax rate (0.02). Revenue guidance ex completed divestitures implies 7%-9% growth.",
  "No organic/constant-currency table; revenue ex Engineering Solutions growth 11% stated in text."
 ],
